# Why is the following code giving me an error?

I am trying to write a program that counts the number of vowels in a string. The program works for the most part, but it gives me an error when I enter the string "aa". I have tried a few different ways of solving this problem, but none of them seem to work. Here is the code that I have written so far:

#include <iostream>
#include <string>

using namespace std;

int main() {
string input;
int count = 0;
cout << "Enter a string: ";
getline(cin, input);
for (int i = 0; i < input.length(); i++) {
if (input[i] == 'a' || input[i] == 'e' || input[i] == 'i' || input[i] == 'o' || input[i] == 'u') {
count++;
}
}
cout << "There are " << count << " vowels in the string." << endl;
return 0;
}


When I enter the string "aa", the program gives me the error "terminate called after throwing an instance of'std::out_of_range'" and then crashes.

